 "title": "27B CPU batched T-row verify (roadmap CP1): exact, and 0.51x against plain decode",
 "measured": "2026-11-26",
 "commit": "a009e64",
 "command": "python tools/cpu_batch_check.py --pack <27B pack> --rows 15 --batch 5 --keep 2 --out check.json; python tools/spec_cpu_bench.py --pack <27B pack> --drafter-pack <2B pack> --tokens 16 --k 4 --prompts 4 --out gate.json",
 "notes": "The CP1 pass (kindi/kcpu.c kc_step_batch + kindi/mtp_cpu.py speculative_decode) was uncommitted in the worktree at measurement time and lands in the commit that adds this claim, on top of a009e64. results.json is the sanitized copy of the two runs (machine paths stripped). The check rows are bit-identical to plain decode (max abs logit delta 0.000e+00) and the rollback lands exactly; the gate's four prompts are token-exact, so the acceptance is measured against the real model. The gate is a MISS: 0.51x mean against the >=1.25x bar, because a 5-row pass costs 4.4 plain rows in isolation (0.59 plain tokens per row inside the loop), not ~1; break-even needs m >= 1.95 of k=4 drafts, the 1.25x bar needs 2.69.",
